bled":false,"open_issues_count":291,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":1172,"open_issues":291,"watchers":7608,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"My mental model has been that a node referencing a mesh _is_ a mesh in the scene graph. A mesh is a node in most engines, I think (it can have a TRS transform) so appending it as a child of a node would just be needless cruft in the scene graph. However, can a single node be more than one (or all) of the following, simultaneously?\r\n\r\n- mesh\r\n- camera\r\n- joint<sup>1</sup>\r\n- light\r\n\r\nI made a quick test of a mesh-camera ([mesh-camera.zip](https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF/files/2317078/mesh-camera.zip)). It passes validation, but the camera is ignored in three.js and BabylonJS.\r\n\r\nIf this is not the intention, we may want to take the step of disallowing use of KHR_lights_punctual on a node that is already a mesh, camera, or joint before ratifying it. \r\n\r\n<sup>1</sup> Not entirely sure if joints belong in this list, since they're somewhat implicit in glTF 2.0.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KhronosGroup/glTF/issues/1433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KhronosGroup/glTF/issues/1433/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":1831011414,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4MzEwMTE0MTQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/events/1831011414","actor":{"login":"donmccurdy","id":1848368,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDgzNjg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1848368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.gi